{title: 101 - Children of the Heavenly Father}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #101 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 101}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F#m]Children of the heavenly Father [A]Safely [A7]in [G]His [F#m]bosom [A7]gather;
[D/A]Nestling [G/D]bird nor star in heaven [F#m]Such a refuge [A7/G]e'er was given.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F#m]God His own doth [A]tend [A7]and [F#m]nourish,
[F#m]In His holy [A]love [A7]they [F#m]flourish;
[D/A]From all [G/D]evil [D]things [F#m]He spares [A7/G]them,
[D/A]In [G/D]His mighty [F#m]arms He [A7/G]bears them.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F#m]Neither life nor [A]death [A7]shall [F#m]ever
[F#m]From the Lord His [A]children [F#m]sever;
[D/A]Unto [G/D]them His [F#m]grace He [A7/G]showeth,
[D/A]And [G/D]their sorrows [F#m]all He [A7/G]knoweth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F#m]Praise the Lord in [A]joyful [F#m]numbers,
[F#m]Your Protector [A]never [F#m]slumbers;
[D/A]At [G/D]the will of [F#m]your Defender
[D/A]Every [G/D]foe-man [F#m]must surrender.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F#m]Though He giveth [A]or [A7]He [F#m]taketh,
[F#m]God His children [A]ne'er [A7]forsaketh;
[D/A]His the [G/D]loving [D]purpose [F#m]solely
[D/A]To [G/D]preserve them [F#m]pure and [A7/G]holy.
{end_of_verse}
